      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-team-2024-p4.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(x\\) is a multiple of 9 , so is \\(999-x\\), and their digits always sum to 27 . The 112 multiples from 0 to 999 form 56 such pairs, so the sum of their digits is \\(56 \\cdot 27=1512\\).",
